# HTML

- Use semantic elements. Use `button` for actions and `a` for navigation.
- Do not make `span` or `div` elements clickable.
- Interactive controls must be usable from the keyboard.
- Add ARIA only when native semantics are not enough.
- Every image needs an appropriate `alt`. Use empty `alt` only when the image is decorative and another control already names it.
- External links opened in a new tab use `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Do not add inline styles or inline event handlers.
- Keep a valid heading hierarchy and do not create duplicate IDs.
- Do not insert unsanitized external HTML.

```html
<!-- Bad -->
<span onclick="openResume()">Resume</span>

<!-- Good -->
<a href="documents/resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resume</a>
```
